# Reconstruction status - 2026-10-24

Target: x86 FreeBSD/GCC3.3.3. SHA256:61fa6e736a5b0ff446dfd817dd9a87a42d2bfbcf5da27b7975cb8ae1e2b67a1c. The supplied 2009 date is not independently authenticated.

## Current recovered scope

Game infrastructure includes FSM, events/queue, vectors, CRC/hash, memory text loader, buffers, traffic profiler, packet registries, exact sequence table, game clock, locale predicates and profiler reporting. Core libraries include heartbeat/runtime/logging,22 utilities, buffers,20 socket functions,12 kqueue functions, signals, memcpy, TEA/XTEA and GOST. libgame grid/attribute bodies are recovered. Per-module notes and evidence retain detailed coverage.

Networking includes partial DESC with complete old data, initialization/destruction, input/output, buffering/encryption, phase/flush, handshake/SyncTime, sequence, UDP/key/CRC and login keys. CLIENT_DESC has complete old data, setup/connect and DB packet writers. DESC_MANAGER has complete old data and initialization/login/handle/handshake registries. Input base/parser/Pong/Handshake and concrete input lifecycle/GetType are recovered; application Analyze handlers remain pending.

CEntity lifecycle/views/observer/spatial traversal and SECTREE initialization/attributes/insertion/removal/neighbor population are recovered. Horse rider addressed functions and base virtual defaults use real event scheduling, with exact31x48-byte stats. Sector ownership/destructor remains pending.

Complete old CHARACTER/CMob data declarations support real GetName, GetCharType, GetRaceNum, ChatPacket and state scheduling. CHARACTER_MANAGER now has real constructor/destructor entry, evidenced empty Destroy, wrapping VID allocation, numeric/PID/typed lookup, name lookup, unique state membership, stone selection and race registration. VID equality checks ID and CRC. Name lookup folds ASCII and uses24 bytes. Race selection prioritizes polymorph, then mob/job, and truncates to WORD. See character-manager-recovery.md and character-chat-recovery.md.

## Validation and limitations

All39 runtime suites and check-abi passed after chat/VID integration. Subsequent name/race additions passed focused manager/name/descriptor-control/entity checks. Name lookup and chat passed optimized checks. Updated character/manager/horse sources pass32-bit syntax checks. validation-status.json records checkpoints. The original binary is never executed.

Modern STL differs from target GCC3.3 containers: full CHARACTER/manager/sector/packet registry ABI equivalence is not claimed. Packed records and supported layouts have structural checks. Host MinGW/C++03 checks do not prove FreeBSD runtime or binary equivalence. Chat retains original unsafe oversized-format semantics; safe-length tests cover up to84 text bytes.

Explicit test-only boundaries include CHARACTER lifecycle/unrecovered protocol virtuals/Disconnect, SECTREE destructor, CLIENT_DESC Destroy/SetPhase, DESC_MANAGER destructor, concrete Analyze and scripted OS/time/event boundaries. Real horse lifecycle, ChatPacket and state scheduling are no longer substitutes.

Most gameplay, database integration, startup and remaining lifecycle/ownership functions remain pending. Full server compile/link and Visual Studio integration are incomplete. Native Windows support is deferred by request. Source reconstruction is incremental, not the original text recovered verbatim.

Inventory174 compilation units/6503 addressed records/5952 distinct starts is not a completion percentage. Decompiled archives remain evidence, not compiled source. Historical notes may describe earlier fixture boundaries; this status supersedes them.


